This distribution contains independent desktop and runtime code under Apache-2.0.
It does not contain the legacy SPELL source library. Qt for Python, debugpy and
Pygments are separately installed dependencies with their own license notices.

The pinned PySide6_Essentials and shiboken6 6.10.3 Linux wheels omit installed
license-text members. This package supplies their direct LGPL-3.0-only,
GPL-2.0-only and GPL-3.0-only texts, together with two upstream Python Software
Foundation attributions, in openbexi_ide/licenses/qt_for_python_6_10_3/.
Its manifest binds each unchanged notice to the official v6.10.3 source commit
and each dependency to the exact Linux wheel bytes. These supplemental notices
do not relicense Qt or replace the corresponding-source requirements or the
separate review of the Qt libraries and third-party components in those wheels.

Procedure identity rules retain the Apache-2.0 legacy OpenBEXI implementation's
UUID namespace and comment metadata behavior. The durable service consciously
migrates its admission and no-automatic-replay rules without importing the legacy
SPELL parser, operational broker or domain services.

The offline Execution release authority retains the legacy OpenBEXI rules for
operator-provisioned immutable releases, exact source/dependency identities and
server-side admission, without its parser, SQLAlchemy or operational DSS broker.
